{"full":"hf:davanstrien/ocr-bench-britannica-results-qwen35-viewer","spaceId":"davanstrien/ocr-bench-britannica-results-qwen35-viewer","name":"OCR Bench: Britannica Results","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","ocr","leaderboard","vlm-judge","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":9,"created":"2026-03-03T15:59:23.000Z","updated":"2026-07-08T15:53:40.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://davanstrien-ocr-bench-britannica-results-qwen35-viewer.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/davanstrien/ocr-bench-britannica-results-qwen35-viewer","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:23.294Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:23.294Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:23.294Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🔍","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["There is currently no single best OCR model. Rankings change depending on your documents. Manuscript cards, printed books, historical texts all produce different winners.","ocr-bench allows you to create per-collection leaderboards using a VLM-as-judge approach, so you can find what works best for your documents rather than relying on generic benchmarks. You can validate the VLM's judgement with human votes, and share results via the Hugging Face Hub.","The underlying OCR model inference uv scripts are available at uv-scripts/ocr. The majority of these use vLLM for efficient GPU inference, and are designed to run on a single consumer GPU (e.g. 24GB 3090/4090). The ocr-bench package orchestrates running these models at scale on the Hub, and judging outputs with a VLM. If you just want to run some OCR models on your data without the judging/leaderboard aspect, you can run the scripts directly."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/davanstrien/ocr-bench-britannica-results-qwen35-viewer/blob/main/README.md","fi